ICML-2025-P0137,ICML-2025-A000640,Ziyad Benomar,stacked,2,4,4,"growth in recent years, starting with the seminal works (Lykouris & Vassilvtiskii, ) and (Purohit et al., ), particularly in online decision making. In this class of problems, the input is a sequence of items, which are revealed one by one, with the algorithm making an irrevocable decision on each. Here, the prediction oracle provides some inherently imperfect information on the input items, which the algorithm must be able to leverage in a judicious manner.",-6,data/raw/icml/2025/first_pages/ICML-2025-P0137.txt,https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mlresearch/v267/main/assets/benomar25a/benomar25a.pdf
