ICML-2025-P0174,ICML-2025-A000824,Andreas Oeldemann,stacked,2,4,5,"(Meinilä et al., ) families are physically oriented and combine physics with statistical channel properties. These models use the laws of electromagnetic wave propagation to describe channels as a function of the corresponding physical parameters (directions of arrival (DoAs), delays, etc.), which in turn are characterized statistically. These characteristics are calibrated and evaluated by real-world measurement campaigns in different propagation scenarios such as indoor, outdoor, urban, and rural (Yin & Cheng, ). While these models characterize channels in generic scenarios and are widely accepted in the communication community, they also exhibit considerable drawbacks.",-6,data/raw/icml/2025/first_pages/ICML-2025-P0174.txt,https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mlresearch/v267/main/assets/bock25a/bock25a.pdf
