ICML-2025-P0659,ICML-2025-A003284,Fabio Feser,stacked,2,2,2,"In genetics, these methods help identify genes associated with disease outcomes. As genes are naturally found in groups (pathways), group selection approaches have been proposed, that allow grouping information to be used, such as the group lasso (Yuan & Lin, ), group SLOPE (Brzyski et al., ), and group SCAD (Guo et al., ). Applying only group shrinkage can harm convergence and prediction, as all variables in an active group are retained, including noise variables (Simon et al., ; Feser & Evangelou, ).",-8,data/raw/icml/2025/first_pages/ICML-2025-P0659.txt,https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mlresearch/v267/main/assets/feser25a/feser25a.pdf
ICML-2025-P0659,ICML-2025-A003285,Marina Evangelou,stacked,2,2,2,"In genetics, these methods help identify genes associated with disease outcomes. As genes are naturally found in groups (pathways), group selection approaches have been proposed, that allow grouping information to be used, such as the group lasso (Yuan & Lin, ), group SLOPE (Brzyski et al., ), and group SCAD (Guo et al., ). Applying only group shrinkage can harm convergence and prediction, as all variables in an active group are retained, including noise variables (Simon et al., ; Feser & Evangelou, ).",-8,data/raw/icml/2025/first_pages/ICML-2025-P0659.txt,https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mlresearch/v267/main/assets/feser25a/feser25a.pdf
