ICML-2025-P1263,ICML-2025-A006415,Steinar Laenen,stacked,2,3,3,"data points in ε− · n0. +o( ) time for the Gaussian kernel1 . In particular, our algorithm maintains ( ± ε)-approximate estimates of the kernel densities for every query point q ∈ Q throughout the sequence of data point insertions; see Theorem . for the formal statement. Although it is known that KDE estimators can be maintained dynamically (Liang et al., ), to the best of our knowledge, this represents the first dynamic algorithm for the KDE problem that efficiently maintains query estimates under data point insertions.",-6,data/raw/icml/2025/first_pages/ICML-2025-P1263.txt,https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mlresearch/v267/main/assets/laenen25a/laenen25a.pdf
