ICML-2025-P1711,ICML-2025-A008831,Emilia Magnani,stacked,2,4,4,"output pairs (Boullé & Townsend, ). Neural operators, including Fourier neural operators, have emerged as a powerful class of models for operator learning, particularly for the solution operators of PDEs (Kovachki et al., ). They have been applied successfully across domains including weather forecasting (Pathak et al., ; Bonev et al., ), fluid dynamics (Grady et al., ; Renn et al., ; Li et al., ), and automotive aerodynamics (Li et al., 2023b). Instead of learning to solve a specific PDE, these models learn the operator that maps a functional parameter of the PDE (such as initial values, boundary conditions, force fields, or material parameters) to the corresponding solution. This approach amortizes computational cost by learning to solve entire families of PDEs.",-4,data/raw/icml/2025/first_pages/ICML-2025-P1711.txt,https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mlresearch/v267/main/assets/magnani25a/magnani25a.pdf
