ICML-2025-P1868,ICML-2025-A009592,Atsushi Nitanda,stacked,2,4,5,"training can now be formulated as the optimization over the space of probability distributions (Nitanda & Suzuki, ). Gradient descent for MFNNs exhibits global convergence (Chizat & Bach, ; Mei et al., ) and adaptivity (Yang & Hu, ; Ba et al., ). To improve stability during training, one may consider noisy gradient training by adding Gaussian noise, giving rise to mean-field Langevin dynamics (MFLD) (Mei et al., ; Hu et al., ). MFLD, with N = ∞, also achieves global convergence to the optimal solution (Hu et al., ; Jabir et al., ), with an exponential convergence rate under the uniform log-Sobolev inequality (LSI) (Nitanda et al., ; Chizat, ) in the continuous-time setting.",-8,data/raw/icml/2025/first_pages/ICML-2025-P1868.txt,https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mlresearch/v267/main/assets/nitanda25a/nitanda25a.pdf
