ICML-2025-P2119,ICML-2025-A010823,Fabian Schaipp,stacked,2,4,5,". Validation Loss We show that learning-rate schedules for large model training behave surprisingly similar to a performance bound from non-smooth convex optimization theory. We provide a bound for the constant schedule with linear cooldown; in particular, the practical benefit of cooldown is reflected in the bound due to the absence of logarithmic terms. Further, we show that this surprisingly close match between optimization theory and practice can be exploited for learning-rate tuning: we achieve noticeable improvements for training 124M and 210M Llama-type models by (i) extending the schedule for continued training with optimal learning-rate, and (ii) transferring the optimal learning-rate across schedules. wsd T ∈ [22k, 33k, 44k] . . . . . cosine T ∈ [22k, 33k, 44k] . Iteration t (a) Real Loss Curves Suboptimality bound",-6,data/raw/icml/2025/first_pages/ICML-2025-P2119.txt,https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mlresearch/v267/main/assets/schaipp25a/schaipp25a.pdf
