ICML-2025-P2140,ICML-2025-A010955,R. Oguz Araz,stacked,2,3,4,"can be present between versions, which go beyond typical augmentations used by the machine learning community. Two musical versions may feature different instrumentation or timbre, together with tonality and chord modifications, altered melodies, substantial changes to rhythm and tempo, an alternate temporal development or structure, and many more (Yesiler et al., ). Yet, musical versions retain their essence, to the point that we can generally agree whether two of them correspond to the same piece or not2 . Therefore, learnt version representations need to encapsulate multiple characteristics shared between versions that, at the same time, can discriminate them from other pieces.",-6,data/raw/icml/2025/first_pages/ICML-2025-P2140.txt,https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mlresearch/v267/main/assets/serra25a/serra25a.pdf
