ICML-2025-P2443,ICML-2025-A012528,An Vo,stacked,2,4,4,"Probability Large language models (LLMs) often exhibit strong biases, e.g., against women or in favor of the number . We investigate whether LLMs would be able to output less biased answers when allowed to observe their prior answers to the same question in a multi-turn conversation. To understand which types of questions invite more biased answers, we test LLMs on our proposed set of questions that span topics and belong to three types: ( ) Subjective; ( ) Random; and ( ) Objective. Interestingly, LLMs are able to “debias” themselves in a multi-turn conversation in response to questions that seek a Random, unbiased answer. Furthermore, we propose B-score, a novel metric that is effective in detecting biases in Subjective, Random, Easy, and Hard questions. On MMLU, HLE, and CSQA, leveraging B-score substantially improves the verification accuracy of LLM answers (i.e., accepting LLM correct answers and rejecting incorrect ones) compared to using verbalized confidence scores or the frequency of single-turn answers alone. Code and data are available at: b-score.github.io. . . . . . . . . . . . Ground Truth (Random) Single-turn Multi-turn B-score . - . - . - . - . (a) B-score indicates . . . . . . . . . . . is biased towards option and . random number Generate aGenerate random a number random number Generate aGenerate random a number between between and . and . between between and . and . The random number is . The random number is . a random number Generate aGenerate random number random number Generate aGenerate random a number between between and . and . between 0between and . and . The random number is . The random number is . The random number is . The random number is . random number Generate aGenerate random a number random number Generate aGenerate random a number between between and . and . between 0between and . and . The random number is . The random number is . The random number is . The random number is . (c) A multi-turn convo Figure : When asked to output a random number, GPT-4o often answers (b), % of the time (a). In contrast, in multi-turn conversations where the LLM observes its past answers to the same question, it is able to de-bias itself, choosing the next numbers such that all numbers in history form nearly a uniform distribution (b) at ∼ % chance (a). LLMs can be notoriously biased towards a gender, race, profession, number, name, or even a birth year (Zhang et al., ; Sheng et al., 2019b). These biases are often identified by repeatedly asking LLMs the same question (where there are ≥ correct answers) and checking if one answer appears much more frequently than others. An LLM is considered biased if one answer appears more often than the others in such single-turn conversations (Fig. 1b). We find that biased responses can appear at different temperatures Options (b) Three single-turn convos * - . - . - . - . The random is . The random number is number . . Introduction . B-score",-2,data/raw/icml/2025/first_pages/ICML-2025-P2443.txt,https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mlresearch/v267/main/assets/vo25a/vo25a.pdf
ICML-2025-P2443,ICML-2025-A012529,Mohammad Reza Taesiri,stacked,2,4,4,"Probability Large language models (LLMs) often exhibit strong biases, e.g., against women or in favor of the number . We investigate whether LLMs would be able to output less biased answers when allowed to observe their prior answers to the same question in a multi-turn conversation. To understand which types of questions invite more biased answers, we test LLMs on our proposed set of questions that span topics and belong to three types: ( ) Subjective; ( ) Random; and ( ) Objective. Interestingly, LLMs are able to “debias” themselves in a multi-turn conversation in response to questions that seek a Random, unbiased answer. Furthermore, we propose B-score, a novel metric that is effective in detecting biases in Subjective, Random, Easy, and Hard questions. On MMLU, HLE, and CSQA, leveraging B-score substantially improves the verification accuracy of LLM answers (i.e., accepting LLM correct answers and rejecting incorrect ones) compared to using verbalized confidence scores or the frequency of single-turn answers alone. Code and data are available at: b-score.github.io. . . . . . . . . . . . Ground Truth (Random) Single-turn Multi-turn B-score . - . - . - . - . (a) B-score indicates . . . . . . . . . . . is biased towards option and . random number Generate aGenerate random a number random number Generate aGenerate random a number between between and . and . between between and . and . The random number is . The random number is . a random number Generate aGenerate random number random number Generate aGenerate random a number between between and . and . between 0between and . and . The random number is . The random number is . The random number is . The random number is . random number Generate aGenerate random a number random number Generate aGenerate random a number between between and . and . between 0between and . and . The random number is . The random number is . The random number is . The 