ICML-2025-P2652,ICML-2025-A013702,Zhongyi Zhou,stacked,2,5,10,"diffusion-vla.github.io Internet-Scale VisionLanguage Data Language Instruction Generalize To Visual Changes Vision Encoder Distractor Large Language Model Reasoning Tokens Action Tokens … … Unseen Background Robot Data with Reasoning Open-Sourced Data Example of Reasoning View Shifting Robot: Pick up the rubik’s cube. Sorting Generalization Robot: Pick up the yellow pepper. Robot: Grabbing the toy blue car. Post Training Data Zero-Shot Bin Picking Interpretability Robot: Grabbing the hex key. Robot: The pot open towards the left. More… Adaptation to New Embodiment Contextual Reasoning Robot: The pot open towards the right. Fast at Inference 82Hz DiVLA-2B 42Hz DiVLA-7B 5Hz OpenVLA-7B Reasoning Injection Module Chatting User: Describe the scene DiVLA: A rubik’s cube is on the right of a yellow object. Diffusion Model User: What is the object? DiVLA: It is not clear, But looks like tulips. Figure : Our proposed DiffusionVLA model unifies autoregressive and diffusion modeling to enable self-reasoning and robot policy learning. This approach generalizes effectively to visual changes, supports zero-shot bin picking, adapts to new robot morphologies, performs visual question-answering, and generates actions with high speed.",-6,data/raw/icml/2025/first_pages/ICML-2025-P2652.txt,https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mlresearch/v267/main/assets/wen25g/wen25g.pdf
