ICML-2025-P2879,ICML-2025-A014967,Yuhan Ye,stacked,2,3,3,"where C ⊂ Rp is a convex set, ξ, ζ ⊂ Ω are random vectors with probability measures Pξ , Pζ , respectively, and G, H : (Rp , Ω) → R are Carathéodory functions, i.e., they are continuous in x for all ξ, ζ ∈ Ω and Borel measurable in ξ and ζ for all x ∈ C. In addition, we assume G and H are convex in x (though not necessarily smooth), making f a difference-of-convex (DC) function.",-6,data/raw/icml/2025/first_pages/ICML-2025-P2879.txt,https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mlresearch/v267/main/assets/ye25c/ye25c.pdf
